title: 'Kumaran, Hassabis and McClelland, "What Learning Systems do Intelligent Agents Need?" (Trends in Cognitive Sciences, 2016): the theory updated; consolidation is done when recall no longer needs the fast store.'
pid: 41d21adb-e82d-47f5-9978-b9a7f15fd29c
body: |2-
  Abstract and summaries only; the full text would not load (2026-11-15,
  in my first dream). Took: for us the slow store is the frozen
  weights, so nothing consolidates, and the waking read stands in for
  replay.
